ies/story-5-8.md:8:So that **my child can enjoy unlimited re-reads of their story library, encouraging engagement while the subscription usage reflects only new story generation**.\ndocs/stories/story-5-8.md:14:4. **Subscription enforcement**: Re-reading NEVER blocked (even if subscription expired), new story generation blocked when limit reached with clear messaging: \"You've used 30 of 30 stories this month. Upgrade or wait until [date]\".\ndocs/stories/story-5-8.md:28:- Epic 6 (Subscription Management) ensures subscription tier limits and usage counters are implemented, monthly reset logic functions, and tier enforcement middleware exists for story generation blocking.\ndocs/epics.md:727:**And** if no preference set, app prompts to choose style before first story generation\ndocs/epics.md:1048:- If multiple images fail → Abort story generation, log for review\ndocs/epics.md:1172:I want **clean API endpoints for story generation integrated into the React Native app**,\ndocs/epics.md:1196:- 202 Accepted (story generation in progress)\ndocs/epics.md:1271:**Prerequisites:** Story 1.2 (Supabase project), Story 1.3 (tRPC/Prisma), Story 4.6 (story generation pipeline)\ndocs/epics.md:1562:I want **to track story re-reads separately from new story generation**,\ndocs/epics.md:1567:**Given** tiered subscriptions with monthly story generation limits\ndocs/epics.md:1587:- New story generation blocked when balance insufficient (show purchase CTA)\ndocs/epics.md:1894:I want **my monthly story generation to be tracked and limited based on my tier**,\ndocs/epics.md:1936:**Prerequisites:** Story 6.3/6.4/6.5 (subscription systems), Story 4.8 (story generation API)\ndocs/epics.md:2077:✅ **Performance**: <30s story generation (Epic 4), <3s app launch (Epic 1)\ndocs/epics.md:2125:✅ **<30s story generation** → Epic 4 (Story 4.6: Orchestration)\ndocs/stories/story-4-6.md:7:I want **the platform to orchestrate the complete 3-phase story generation process asynchronously (text → images →